 "function": "cloudgen.texture.regime_texture",
 "doc": "Plans in call order: 0-1 the generic fBm (seed+3, directions 0.75 p + 0.25 back), 2-3 the street fBm (seed+5, 0.1 p + 0.9 back), then a (worley3, cell_edges) pair for each USED cell diameter (seed + int(d_km), directions 0.85 p + 0.15 back); params.cells_used_km lists them, the fBm ladder is octave_ladder(fine_frequency, fmax) (the plans hold its result). The cells are accumulated in float32 and standardized over the WHOLE array (a global mean and std: the case is one array). A 64x32 grid of float32 directions with hand-built back-traced directions and the weights regime_weights gives for Earth (float64). Earth at 4096 wide: radius 6371, fmax 326: the 15 km cells (f = 424 > fmax) hit the `continue` branch, 30/60/120 km are used, the ladder has 3 octaves up to 310 cycles/rad. The texture is a float32 chain whose coordinates reach 300, so one float32 ulp of a direction moves a noise coordinate by 2e-5: measured worst difference 6.2e-4 against an all-float64 evaluation of the same plans (99.9% of texels below 3.3e-4) and 7.7e-4 when p, back and the weights move by one float32 ulp; tolerance atol 8e-3, rtol 1e-5 (10x). Outputs besides `texture` are the intermediates, there to localize a mismatch: generic_std and street_std (the standardized fBm fields), and, when a cell diameter is used, closed_sum and open_sum (the float32 weighted sums of the cell ramps, before standardization) and closed_std / open_std (their standardizations); each has its own measured tolerance, see TEX_INTER in the case module. params.constants holds the mixes, ramps and seed offsets written in the code, and params.cells_per_radian the f = radius_km / d_km compared with fmax for each diameter (`f > fmax` skips, a tie f == fmax is USED; f is computed by a division).",
